This repository is a throughline *source*: a requirements graph, not a program. It
re-expresses the NCSC Cyber Assessment Framework (CAF) version 4.0 as a grounded IDD graph
so consuming projects can compose it with throughline-compose.

The CAF content re-expressed here — the four Objective descriptions (each intent's `text`),
the fourteen Principle statements (each user_requirement's `rationale`), the Contributing
Outcome statements (each system_requirement's `text`) and the Indicators of Good Practice
(each system_requirement's `attrs.igp_*` lists) — is taken from:

  - NCSC Cyber Assessment Framework 4.0 —
    https://www.ncsc.gov.uk/files/NCSC-Cyber-Assessment-Framework-4.0.pdf
  - The CAF collection —
    https://www.ncsc.gov.uk/collection/cyber-assessment-framework

